// Ch6 B06 "After the barge" (act1_ch06.md; W06). In-engine. The wrights are led away up the shoals
// toward the Corrow road under escort, unbranded, their camp still burning behind them. Toma is
// radiant, with tears he doesn't wipe. Liss, in profile, watching the wrights go, says the chapter's
// only dissent, once the barge has gone (W06_after: the escort in the background, Liss in profile).
// Nobody answers it: the silence is held, and Toma's smile holds, then doesn't quite. Then the joining (~60 words), and Asha's tell (when hurting, ask about
// the other's day). The chapter flow seats Liss in the party after this scene.
title: ch06_after_barge
location: ch06/brine_shoals
---
@camera W06_after
@music liss_theme fade=2.0
@mark wrights way_tents_s walk via=way_wrights_n
@face toma tender 0.5
Toma [smile]: You saw him. That is the Order. That is what it is for. #line:ch06_after_001
@anim liss look_at wrights
@wait 1.0
Liss [cold]: He put the fire out once it had finished. #line:ch06_after_002
@wait 2.5
@face toma neutral 1.5
@wait 1.0
Liss [neutral]: Your papers get me past the Corrow checkpoints. I'll pull my weight, and I'll stop when we're square. #line:ch06_after_003
Toma [neutral]: You are written in, Mistress Varrow. You are under my papers now. #line:ch06_after_004
Liss [neutral]: Lucky me. #line:ch06_after_005
Ysolde [soft_smile]: Welcome to the Lady Cantor's party. #line:ch06_after_006
@mark asha toma_apart walk via=way_camp_e
@anim asha look_at toma
Asha [tender]: Are you all right? #line:ch06_after_007
Toma [smile]: I am better than all right. #line:ch06_after_008
@wait 1.0
<<set $ch06_liss_joined = true>>
===
